I am back in my flat.
I take my new clothes out of the backpack.
First, I try on the green jacket.
The jacket fits perfectly.
It is light and very comfortable.
Then I take the yellow T-shirt.
I pull it over my head.
Oh no, the T-shirt is much too tight.
It is too small at the shoulders.
I quickly take the yellow T-shirt off again.
I fetch an old T-shirt from my closet.
I lay both T-shirts on the bed.
The new T-shirt is clearly smaller than my old T-shirt.
I definitely need a size larger.
I look for the receipt in my backpack.
Fortunately, it is still there.
I pack the T-shirt back up.
I am riding right back to the city center.
I have to exchange the T-shirt.
